---
title: "Fantasy creator"
note: "A fantasy character for Krea 2: a human or one of sixty peoples beyond them (elves, dwarves, orcs, tieflings, cat-, raven- and lizardfolk, minotaurs, centaurs, harpies, ghosts, elementals, golems, treefolk …), each with its own body, so a golem rolls no hairstyle and a ghost no gender. A class brings its clothes and its gear, a wizard or a witch often a familiar; a motif in the signature colour sits on the clothes. It keeps what the picture cannot show (EXPORT:): the people, the class, the gear, the familiar, a mood, a quirk, two skills, a voice, so a reel that casts it from the gallery reads $hero.people, $hero.gear and $hero.voice. One seed is one character, from four sides by the grid: the close views show the head, the shoulders and the clothes, the full-length view the gear and the familiar too; $backdrop puts it in its world instead of the studio, $view one side only to try characters faster."
tags: [krea, characters, references, fantasy]
---
$colour = __characters/creator/colour__
$people = __characters/fantasy/people__
$gender = {IF $people.gender is no: none|{woman:4|man:4|person}}
$fit = {IF $gender is woman: women|{IF $gender is man: men|all}}
$age = {young:3|seasoned:3|grizzled:2|venerable|timeworn}
$build = __characters/creator/build__
$face = __characters/creator/face__
$eyes = __characters/creator/eyes__
$haircolour = {__characters/creator/haircolour__:5|silver-white|$colour-dyed|ash-grey}
$hair = __characters/creator/hair[fit=$fit|all]__
$beard = {IF $people.beard is yes: {IF $gender is man: {__characters/creator/beard__:3|none:2}|none}|none}
$mark = __characters/creator/mark__
$class = __characters/fantasy/class__
$gear = $class.gear
$motif = __characters/creator/motif[genre=fantasy|all]__
$familiar = {IF $class.familiar is often: {__characters/creator/companion[genre=fantasy]__:2|none}|{__characters/creator/companion[genre=fantasy]__|none:4}}
$presence = __characters/creator/presence__
$backdrop = {studio:3|world}
# A people takes the parts its body has: a human-like one face, eyes, hair and a mark; beastfolk their eyes; spirits and constructs only their own look.
$folk = {IF $gender is none: $age $people|$age $people $gender}
$body = {IF $people.like is human: $people.look, $build, $face, $eyes, $hair{IF $beard is not none: , $beard|} and $mark|{IF $people.like is beast: {IF $people.eyes is own: $people.look|$people.look, $eyes}|$people.look}}
$person = a $folk with $body: $class in $class.wear, their clothes marked by $motif
$who = $person, with $gear{IF $familiar is not none: , $familiar|}
# What the picture carries beyond its prompt (EXPORT:): a screenplay that casts it reads $hero.who, $hero.people, $hero.gear …
EXPORT:
  who = $who
  $people
  $gender
  age = $age
  $class
  gear = $gear
  familiar = $familiar
  $colour
  mood = __characters/creator/mood__
  quirk = __characters/creator/quirk__
  skills = {2$$__characters/creator/skill[genre=fantasy|all]__}
  voice = __characters/creator/voice__
# The grid runs every view: one character from four sides. Set $view to one of them to try characters faster.
# The shot comes first and the picture names only what it can show: the close views the head, the shoulders and the clothes; the full-length view the gear too, and the familiar in a sentence of its own.
$look = {photo:4|animated:2|anime:2|painted:2}
$view = {portrait|three-quarter|full-length|profile}
$opening = {IF $look is photo: A cinematic photograph, as from the set of a fantasy film|{IF $look is animated: A 3D character render, in the style of a modern animated feature film|{IF $look is anime: An anime character design|A gouache fantasy character study}}}
$shot = {IF $view is portrait: a head-and-shoulders portrait|{IF $view is three-quarter: a head-and-shoulders view|{IF $view is full-length: a full-length view of the whole body, from the top of the head to the feet,|a strict side profile of the head and shoulders}}}
$stand = They stand straight with the arms relaxed, facing the camera, with $gear, and floor and space around them are in frame.
$pose = {IF $view is portrait: They face the camera.|{IF $view is three-quarter: They are turned three-quarters to the left.|{IF $view is full-length: {IF $familiar is not none: $stand With them: $familiar.|$stand}|The face is seen exactly from the side, turned 90 degrees to the left, the nose pointing at the left edge of the frame and only one eye visible.}}}
$finish = {IF $look is photo: Shot on an 85mm lens at eye level, true colours, practical costume and makeup.|{IF $look is animated: Stylised proportions, soft subsurface skin.|{IF $look is anime: Clean line art and flat cel shading.|Visible brush strokes on warm paper.}}}
$opening: $shot of $person, with $presence. $pose Behind them is {IF $backdrop is studio: a seamless mid-grey studio backdrop|__characters/fantasy/realm__}, in soft, even light. $finish
@size 832x1216
@grid $view
